      "quoted_tweet": {
        "type": "tweet",
        "id": "2053180880383041547",
        "url": "https://x.com/GmaIndiana/status/2053180880383041547",
        "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/GmaIndiana/status/2053180880383041547",
        "text": "April 28, 1968 - Thừa Thiên Province, Vietnam.\nRonnie Glynn Slay, a 20-year-old from Houston, Texas, had only just arrived in Vietnam on March 3, 1968. Drafted into service, he barely had time to settle into the reality of war before it found him.\nAssigned to Charlie Company, Ist Battalion, 501st Infantry Regiment, 101st Airborne Division — one of the Screaming Eagles — he was an infantryman on the front lines almost immediately.\nA young Texan.\nAn Airborne soldier.\nA man asked to carry more than most ever should, far from home.\nOn April 28, 1968, in Thừa Thiên Province, his life was taken by enemy small arms fire.\nJust weeks after arriving.\nOnly 20 years old.\nA future left unfinished.\n\nToday and everyday we remember Private First Class\nRonnie Glynn Slay. 🇺🇸",
